1
00:00:00,660 --> 00:00:04,800
There was a time when Jaguar was one of the
most admired names in the car industry.

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:07,000
Its cars were breathtaking.

3
00:00:07,430 --> 00:00:09,200
Its racers conquered Le Mans.

4
00:00:09,510 --> 00:00:13,400
Its badge represented British elegance, with
a dangerous edge.

5
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:17,411
Today, that same company has stopped making
petrol cars,

6
00:00:17,411 --> 00:00:20,700
and gambled everything on an electric
reinvention.

7
00:00:21,280 --> 00:00:25,600
How did Jaguar go from building legends to
fighting for a new identity?

8
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:29,900
To understand the fall, we need to go back
to 1922.

9
00:00:30,100 --> 00:00:33,635
Two young entrepreneurs, William Lyons and
William Walmsley,

10
00:00:33,635 --> 00:00:37,700
started a business making motorcycle
sidecars in Blackpool, England.

11
00:00:38,170 --> 00:00:40,900
It was the beginning of a luxury empire.

12
00:00:41,130 --> 00:00:43,100
Lyons had an instinct for design.

13
00:00:43,380 --> 00:00:47,167
By 1935, the first Jaguar-badged car had
arrived:

14
00:00:47,167 --> 00:00:50,800
stylish, powerful and surprisingly
affordable.

15
00:00:51,110 --> 00:00:55,200
After the Second World War, the company
officially became Jaguar Cars.

16
00:00:55,500 --> 00:00:58,500
Then, in 1948, everything changed.

17
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:02,044
The XK120 arrived with flowing bodywork and
a top speed

18
00:01:02,044 --> 00:01:05,700
that made it one of the fastest production
cars in the world.

19
00:01:06,450 --> 00:01:09,000
But Jaguar wanted to prove its speed.

20
00:01:09,180 --> 00:01:12,800
In 1951, a Jaguar won the 24 Hours of Le
Mans.

21
00:01:13,120 --> 00:01:14,900
It won again in 1953.

22
00:01:15,400 --> 00:01:18,639
Then came three consecutive victories,

23
00:01:18,639 --> 00:01:22,900
from 1955 to 1957, with the extraordinary
D-Type.

24
00:01:23,400 --> 00:01:28,267
Jaguar was developing aerodynamics and disc
brakes under brutal racing conditions,

25
00:01:28,267 --> 00:01:30,700
earning a reputation money couldn't buy.

26
00:01:31,150 --> 00:01:33,100
And then came 1961.

27
00:01:33,200 --> 00:01:37,775
The Jaguar E-Type: long bonnet, low roof,
sculpted curves,

28
00:01:37,775 --> 00:01:44,400
almost 150 miles an hour of performance for
far less money than many exotic rivals.

29
00:01:44,780 --> 00:01:46,400
It was a cultural phenomenon.

30
00:01:46,890 --> 00:01:50,673
Jaguar had cracked an impossible formula:
race-car excitement,

31
00:01:50,673 --> 00:01:54,700
genuine luxury, at a price that made the
dream feel within reach.

32
00:01:55,140 --> 00:01:58,400
The company followed that elegance with
saloons like the XJ.

33
00:01:58,400 --> 00:02:01,800
Its identity was clear: grace, space and
pace.

34
00:02:02,100 --> 00:02:04,400
But success didn't guarantee stability.

35
00:02:05,180 --> 00:02:10,600
During the late 1960s, Jaguar was swept into
the giant British Leyland group.

36
00:02:10,840 --> 00:02:15,900
Industrial turmoil, financial problems and
quality concerns shook confidence.

37
00:02:16,220 --> 00:02:19,300
The badge survived, but the business was
vulnerable.

38
00:02:19,540 --> 00:02:21,500
There were flashes of brilliance.

39
00:02:21,790 --> 00:02:25,165
Jaguar regained independence in 1984,

40
00:02:25,165 --> 00:02:30,000
and its racing cars won at Le Mans in 1988
and 1990.

41
00:02:30,210 --> 00:02:32,400
Yet the world around it was changing.

42
00:02:32,670 --> 00:02:37,290
BMW, Mercedes-Benz and Audi invested heavily
in technology,

43
00:02:37,290 --> 00:02:40,500
quality and ever-expanding model ranges.

44
00:02:40,640 --> 00:02:44,300
Ford bought Jaguar in 1989 and pushed for
growth.

45
00:02:44,540 --> 00:02:47,766
Models like the S-Type and X-Type reached
new buyers,

46
00:02:47,766 --> 00:02:51,600
but chasing volume made the brand's identity
harder to define.

47
00:02:52,180 --> 00:02:55,100
In 2008, Tata Motors took ownership.

48
00:02:55,180 --> 00:02:57,781
Jaguar fought back with cars like the XF,

49
00:02:57,781 --> 00:03:00,700
the supercharged F-Type and later the
F-Pace.

50
00:03:00,950 --> 00:03:06,100
The all-electric I-Pace showed Jaguar could
still be ambitious.

51
00:03:06,140 --> 00:03:09,600
Some were excellent, but being good wasn't
enough.

52
00:03:10,470 --> 00:03:13,200
Jaguar couldn't match German rivals' scale.

53
00:03:13,710 --> 00:03:18,200
Even within JLR, Range Rover and Defender
became stronger sellers.

54
00:03:18,420 --> 00:03:19,800
The numbers tell the story.

55
00:03:20,430 --> 00:03:26,600
Jaguar sold more than 180,000 vehicles in
the 2018–2019 financial year.

56
00:03:26,970 --> 00:03:30,900
Just five years later, that figure was under
67,000.

57
00:03:31,370 --> 00:03:34,063
And instead of trying to save the old
formula,

58
00:03:34,063 --> 00:03:37,400
Jaguar made a staggering decision: it would
start again.

59
00:03:37,740 --> 00:03:41,100
In 2024, familiar models were discontinued.

60
00:03:41,520 --> 00:03:48,400
In December 2025, the final petrol-powered
Jaguar left the production line.

61
00:03:49,130 --> 00:03:52,069
The brand that once defined the British
sports

62
00:03:52,069 --> 00:03:55,200
car was temporarily building no new cars at
all.

63
00:03:55,780 --> 00:03:58,800
Its 2024 rebrand only intensified the
debate.

64
00:03:59,300 --> 00:04:03,700
Bright colours, a new visual identity, and
an advert without a single car.

65
00:04:04,080 --> 00:04:08,900
Some called it fearless. Others, a betrayal
of Jaguar's heritage.

66
00:04:09,450 --> 00:04:12,700
Then came the radical Type 00 concept,

67
00:04:13,210 --> 00:04:17,123
and in October 2026, Jaguar finally revealed
the Type 01:

68
00:04:17,123 --> 00:04:24,400
an electric four-door grand tourer with more
than a thousand horsepower and a starting
price of £130,000.

69
00:04:25,100 --> 00:04:28,100
It's a bold gamble: rather than chase
volume,

70
00:04:28,100 --> 00:04:30,900
Jaguar now wants exclusive luxury buyers.

71
00:04:31,370 --> 00:04:35,400
But power figures and daring designs can't
automatically rebuild trust.

72
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:38,900
The Type 01 isn't scheduled to reach
customers until 2027.

73
00:04:39,500 --> 00:04:41,600
Its real success is still unproven.

74
00:04:41,990 --> 00:04:45,600
Maybe Jaguar is about to pull off the
greatest comeback in British motoring,

75
00:04:45,910 --> 00:04:49,900
or maybe its golden age will remain exactly
where it began: in the past.

76
00:04:50,440 --> 00:04:51,400
One thing is certain:

77
00:04:51,710 --> 00:04:54,583
the company that once taught the world what
a beautiful,

78
00:04:54,583 --> 00:04:59,200
fast car can be now has to convince the
world to fall in love with Jaguar all over
again.

